WEBVTT

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:57.500
Dan!

00:01:57.500 --> 00:01:58.500
Okay!

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:25.600
Target sensors locked.

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:40.690
Over again?

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:44.360
When am I even gonna
get a chance with SARG 4?

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:45.360
Quit complaining.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:47.630
Good work, team!

00:02:47.630 --> 00:02:50.780
Another alien crushed by Funeral!

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:04.010
I was shocked.

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:07.780
I saw my neighbor Smith's home was stomped on by an alien.

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:38.080
A little like Miranda, daughter of Prospero.

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:41.140
Discovering the world outside the island.

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:46.190
So, what's your impression of this brave new world?

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:51.430
Second Lt. Ryu Soma reporting for duty.

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:53.200
Michael Hartland.

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:55.100
Welcome to the team.

00:03:55.900 --> 00:03:58.270
Captain Michael Hartland.

00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:00.400
Graduated top of his class.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:03.010
Seen plenty of active duty.

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:08.000
Yet look how deferential he is,
walking with a younger officer.

00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:12.240
What's really happening here?

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:27.360
This is your first glimpse, right?

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:28.330
No.

00:04:29.630 --> 00:04:30.760
On TV.

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:36.570
First Lt. Dan Simmons. British.

00:04:36.570 --> 00:04:39.680
The prized son of a noble family.

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:43.250
However, he's in alien
extermination for some reason.

00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:47.440
Oh, my Great Britain.
A tough breed to understand.

00:04:55.490 --> 00:04:57.030
You're not a child.

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:59.360
Why are you running in the halls?

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:02.590
And that looks like $50 worth of junk food.

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:05.370
Second Lt. Sue Harris.

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:06.930
Not big on protocol.

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:12.870
But put her in a cockpit and the kid's a genius.

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:14.910
What's this?

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:16.150
The lock up.

00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:17.380
Lock up?

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:19.720
Where the EX-1 is, the alien specimen

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:22.420
some rogue scientists re-animated.

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:26.220
You saw the report, right?

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:28.190
It's a mysterious case.

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:31.820
It seems there were three of them in on it.

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:34.560
Does that interest you?

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:36.570
Not really.

00:05:42.510 --> 00:05:44.610
First Lt. Guenevere Green.

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:47.910
She's served under Commander Ines
since the Air Force.

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:50.250
She's got a sharp shooting arm,

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:53.410
smooth and steady, like a painter with a brush.

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:04.250
And I believe you've already met Commander Ines.

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:09.420
No, it was Takuto Kaneshiro who did.

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:21.580
Anyway, she's the top dog at this little squad...

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:25.550
...of special alien police known for some reason as "Funeral."

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:29.350
I think you'll enjoy watching them work.

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:38.730
At least, for now.

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:41.490
Welcome aboard, Lt. Ryu Soma.

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:45.500
Want an apple?

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:51.210
Here.

00:06:55.580 --> 00:06:57.880
Don't you want to enjoy it?

00:06:57.880 --> 00:07:01.280
Or are you that sure you won't like the blend?

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:02.250
I'm sure.

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:07.220
Second Lt. Ryu Soma.

00:07:07.220 --> 00:07:10.190
Stratospheric interceptor test pilot...

00:07:10.190 --> 00:07:13.760
...for the 21st regimen in Alaska.

00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:18.010
He had an accident on vacation in March and temporarily retired.

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:22.150
He got himself reassigned to Funeral
when he returned to duty.

00:07:23.110 --> 00:07:23.980
Why?

00:07:23.980 --> 00:07:26.110
To investigate, I guess.

00:07:26.110 --> 00:07:28.550
This magic emblem can unlock doors.

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:30.090
That can't be it.

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:33.200
You can see it on his face.

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:43.530
Well, we'll find out in the simulator.

00:07:43.530 --> 00:07:45.430
Whether he's just a recruit or not.

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:11.450
I'm here.

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:07.170
Maintenance check.

00:10:07.170 --> 00:10:09.440
Group A to check fences.

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:13.040
Group B to check surveillance cameras.

00:10:13.040 --> 00:10:18.050
Proceed with sound proofing,
then report to team leaders.

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:22.350
Once again, Group A to check fences.

00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:58.420
Has he ever done space flight testing?

00:10:58.420 --> 00:10:59.560
He shouldn't have.

00:10:59.560 --> 00:11:01.920
Excellent maneuvering for a first timer.

00:11:24.610 --> 00:11:25.720
Time?

00:11:25.720 --> 00:11:26.850
2:38.

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:29.010
That's a new record.

00:11:31.150 --> 00:11:32.860
That simulation model...

00:11:32.860 --> 00:11:34.760
I can duplicate it here.

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:43.530
What's he doing?

00:11:43.530 --> 00:11:45.900
The champion wants his belt back.

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:55.750
I have a system error.

00:11:55.750 --> 00:11:56.710
No error!

00:11:59.250 --> 00:12:00.880
I'm your next opponent!

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:39.120
A misfire?

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:43.990
It's a technical knock out.

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:47.160
Saved by the bell. Come down, Lt. Soma.

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:49.870
Too bad.

00:12:49.870 --> 00:12:52.960
A misfire routine wasn't in the simulator before.

00:12:56.240 --> 00:12:58.270
You set me up.

00:12:58.270 --> 00:13:01.250
We're on the same side, remember?

00:13:17.430 --> 00:13:18.690
Look!

00:13:18.690 --> 00:13:20.560
It's a new picture book!

00:13:22.130 --> 00:13:23.670
Let's read it together.

00:13:23.670 --> 00:13:25.070
Later.

00:13:25.070 --> 00:13:27.300
You really like drawing, don't you?

00:13:27.300 --> 00:13:29.270
What's that supposed to be?

00:13:29.270 --> 00:13:30.610
A fairy.

00:13:30.610 --> 00:13:32.210
Again?

00:13:32.210 --> 00:13:34.780
So what kind of fairy this time?

00:13:34.780 --> 00:13:36.480
A lot I've seen before.

00:13:38.350 --> 00:13:42.990
Well, if you won't read it,
I guess I'll take it away.

00:13:42.990 --> 00:13:44.290
Don't, Sue!

00:13:44.290 --> 00:13:46.290
I'm leaving with it.

00:13:46.290 --> 00:13:47.420
Don't!

00:13:47.420 --> 00:13:49.260
You can't!

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:50.190
Sue!

00:14:38.570 --> 00:14:41.130
Well, well. Tired already?

00:14:43.380 --> 00:14:44.450
You again?

00:14:44.450 --> 00:14:47.680
Have you met that special someone yet?

00:14:47.680 --> 00:14:50.290
Your silence speaks volumes.

00:14:50.290 --> 00:14:52.490
But I should tell you to be careful.

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:54.390
Rumors are spreading.

00:14:54.390 --> 00:14:57.790
If you don't fall in line,
you can expect problems.

00:14:57.790 --> 00:15:00.730
Oh Father, forgive us our sins.

00:15:00.730 --> 00:15:01.700
What's that mean?

00:15:10.870 --> 00:15:12.570
Hello, darling.

00:15:13.980 --> 00:15:15.640
Not interested in games?

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:18.010
I bet you're more interested...

00:15:18.010 --> 00:15:22.120
...in knowing what the unit's uncovered about Morgue.

00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:24.720
Take a bite from the forbidden fruit.

00:15:24.720 --> 00:15:27.460
It's a sweet fruit from the tree of knowledge

00:15:27.460 --> 00:15:29.790
in the data library.

00:15:53.450 --> 00:15:56.750
It's like Dr. Faust and Mephistopheles.

00:15:56.750 --> 00:15:58.920
Bargaining for the devil's power.

00:15:58.920 --> 00:16:01.420
But it's what you get in return.

00:16:01.420 --> 00:16:03.220
That's the fun part.

00:16:04.690 --> 00:16:05.890
I don't care.

00:16:12.370 --> 00:16:16.040
Meetings of cultures such as the Incas and Spain

00:16:16.040 --> 00:16:18.470
cannot be allowed to be repeated.

00:16:18.470 --> 00:16:20.200
That's why this project...

00:16:24.910 --> 00:16:28.920
Humans are inherently frail.
Powerless creatures on their own.

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:34.860
It is through cooperation that our
species excelled on this planet.

00:16:34.860 --> 00:16:37.390
Contact will not alter evolution.

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:41.800
Meeting guarantees
neither fortune nor misfortune.

00:16:41.800 --> 00:16:43.000
So we project...

00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:43.600
Hey.
So we project...

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:44.600
So we project...

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:45.380
What?
...for an idea.

00:16:45.380 --> 00:16:45.870
...for an idea.

00:16:45.870 --> 00:16:48.100
Air cart riding with Rick.

00:16:48.100 --> 00:16:49.070
Want to come?

00:16:49.070 --> 00:16:51.470
But I'm in the middle of class.

00:16:51.470 --> 00:16:53.040
He took attendance, right?

00:16:53.040 --> 00:16:54.710
You there.

00:16:54.710 --> 00:16:57.210
The one next to Maki Agata!

00:16:58.050 --> 00:17:01.820
Tell us what happens
when alien cultures collide.

00:17:01.820 --> 00:17:04.950
What is the most probable outcome?

00:17:04.950 --> 00:17:07.860
Well, I... Uh, that is...

00:17:07.860 --> 00:17:08.900
Well?

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:11.930
War.

00:17:11.930 --> 00:17:13.560
Why is that?

00:17:13.560 --> 00:17:17.430
Because living things fear
what they don't understand.

00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:20.400
And how does fear lead to war?

00:17:20.400 --> 00:17:25.310
It's a simple matter to attack first and ask questions later.

00:17:25.310 --> 00:17:28.810
In a micro-view,
antibodies and white blood cells...

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:31.850
...are programmed to attack invaders.

00:17:32.620 --> 00:17:33.820
I see.

00:17:33.820 --> 00:17:38.150
So we humans are no better than single-cell organisms?

00:17:38.150 --> 00:17:39.120
No.

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:43.830
Humans have knowledge and understanding.

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:46.030
There's always the chance humans...

00:17:46.030 --> 00:17:48.100
...may overcome fear.

00:17:48.100 --> 00:17:49.430
Interesting.

00:17:49.430 --> 00:17:52.300
So intellect defeats instinct.

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:54.400
A very romantic idea.

00:17:54.400 --> 00:17:57.610
Religions, borders, and slave treaties,

00:17:57.610 --> 00:18:02.610
these are born from intellect,
but they are also causes of wars.

00:18:02.610 --> 00:18:03.440
Well...

00:18:03.440 --> 00:18:04.580
Enough!

00:18:04.580 --> 00:18:08.080
Takuto Kaneshiro from Space Engineering...

00:18:09.150 --> 00:18:13.060
...this is a class about cross-cultural contact.

00:18:13.060 --> 00:18:17.460
Explore the subject of cross-gender
contact on your own time.

00:18:21.030 --> 00:18:24.400
If you had shown up,
I wouldn't have had to sneak in.

00:18:24.400 --> 00:18:28.770
Anyway, the professor said he found
your thesis very interesting.

00:18:28.770 --> 00:18:29.640
My thesis?

00:18:29.640 --> 00:18:32.880
The paper you wrote
about the psychological shift

00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:35.410
that living in space has brought about.

00:18:35.410 --> 00:18:38.910
I told you it was a piece of crap.

00:18:39.520 --> 00:18:41.020
But...

00:18:41.020 --> 00:18:43.850
I thought you made some good points.

00:18:43.850 --> 00:18:45.050
So did Professor.

00:18:45.050 --> 00:18:47.000
I don't care what he said!

00:18:48.420 --> 00:18:50.590
Shutting up again?

00:18:50.590 --> 00:18:52.650
How can I tell what you're thinking?

00:19:09.140 --> 00:19:10.610
That's a lie!

00:19:10.610 --> 00:19:13.620
Dr. Noguchi kept a file on the school server

00:19:13.620 --> 00:19:15.380
about you for a year!

00:19:35.570 --> 00:19:37.910
These aren't right.

00:19:37.910 --> 00:19:40.800
Bad habit for a new recruit.

00:19:41.350 --> 00:19:42.770
What are you looking at?

00:19:44.980 --> 00:19:46.810
How can I tell what you're thinking?

00:19:48.450 --> 00:19:49.990
What's so funny?

00:19:49.990 --> 00:19:52.860
Just remembering a creep I knew.

00:19:52.860 --> 00:19:53.820
Sorry.

00:19:53.820 --> 00:19:57.670
I just thought I had free access
to your databanks.

00:19:58.790 --> 00:20:00.590
Officially, yes, but...

00:20:23.090 --> 00:20:26.590
Early warning radars activated in the 67th quadrant.

00:20:26.590 --> 00:20:30.350
New York coastal region, E-565 by S-221.

00:20:31.360 --> 00:20:34.500
Moving below water at 50 km per hour.

00:20:34.500 --> 00:20:36.470
Landing in 42 minutes.

00:20:36.470 --> 00:20:38.970
We're lucky that area's deserted.

00:20:38.970 --> 00:20:42.240
That's where the first strike was when the war began.

00:20:42.240 --> 00:20:46.580
I doubt it's looking for a date with the Statue of Liberty.

00:20:46.580 --> 00:20:48.770
Their objectives are always the same.

00:20:49.810 --> 00:20:51.350
What's the condition?

00:20:51.350 --> 00:20:53.200
Yellow. Full military alert.

00:20:54.180 --> 00:20:55.050
Captain!

00:20:55.620 --> 00:20:56.950
Ma'am.

00:20:56.950 --> 00:20:58.890
Prepare to move out.

00:20:58.890 --> 00:21:00.260
Second Lt. Soma.

00:21:00.260 --> 00:21:01.220
Yes, sir.

00:21:01.220 --> 00:21:03.130
You stay in the control room.

00:21:03.130 --> 00:21:04.750
Observe how we operate.

00:21:06.300 --> 00:21:07.700
Understood.

00:21:07.700 --> 00:21:09.050
Good. Let's go.

00:21:13.740 --> 00:21:14.700
Captain.

00:21:15.800 --> 00:21:17.600
You'll be all right, won't you?

00:21:17.600 --> 00:21:21.900
We've done our best so far,
and we'll keep on doing it.

00:21:22.780 --> 00:21:24.640
We won't have to use "it" yet.

00:21:25.780 --> 00:21:26.750
Good luck.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:34.910
The Meeting and Hatred

00:22:36.420 --> 00:22:38.110
A decision must be made.

00:22:39.150 --> 00:22:40.990
For as they say,

00:22:40.990 --> 00:22:43.890
he who lives by the sword
may also die by the sword.

00:22:45.930 --> 00:22:48.620
Next time,
Hatred and War.
